feat(scan): scan an image from its registry, and set how far bases may move

Scanner.ScanRemoteImage runs the vulnerability stage over an image read
straight from its registry (trivy image --image-src remote), so a
candidate base image is measured without being pulled into the local
engine. It honours the scan options (server, ignore-unfixed,
ignore-EOL), runs no other stage, and in container mode mounts no engine
socket. Measured on Trivy 0.74.0.

scan.base_image_track (same-line by default, or next-major) sets how far
remediation may move a base image. It is written on load so the
configuration view has a value to cycle from, and an unknown value is
left alone and read as same-line. It is a cycle field in the scan tab.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED
EOF
